<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>救生艇新闻：博客——保护人类</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/</link><description></description><lastBuildDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 15:20:45 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>宗教学者会见人类。他们所听到的让他们震惊</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/religious-scholars-met-with-anthropic-what-they-heard-stunned-them</link><description>如果我们创造的为我们服务的人工智能被证明是有意识的怎么办？ &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/religious-scholars-met-with-anthropic-what-they-heard-stunned-them.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 15:20:42 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/religious-scholars-met-with-anthropic-what-they-heard-stunned-them</guid></item><item><title>1 型糖尿病中的免疫逃避 β 细胞：基因工程、生物材料和计算模型的创新</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/immune-evasive-beta-cells-in-type-1-diabetes-innovations-in-genetic-engineering-biomaterials-and-computational-modeling</link><description>1 型糖尿病 (T1D) 是一种自身免疫性疾病，分泌胰岛素的 β 细胞被免疫细胞破坏，导致血糖水平升高。 β细胞位于胰腺内的朗格汉斯岛，负责产生一种称为胰岛素的重要激素。由于缺乏胰岛素，T1D 患者会出现高血糖，从而导致心脏病、中风、神经损伤和肾衰竭等严重并发症。 T1D 在儿童期或青春期发生，但也可能发生在成人中，其中疾病的发作和进展是由环境或免疫事件触发的。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/immune-evasive-beta-cells-in-type-1-diabetes-innovations-in-genetic-engineering-biomaterials-and-computational-modeling.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 15:05:42 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/immune-evasive-beta-cells-in-type-1-diabetes-innovations-in-genetic-engineering-biomaterials-and-computational-modeling</guid></item><item><title>刘易斯·达特内尔谈起源：地球如何塑造人类历史</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/lewis-dartnell-on-origins-how-the-earth-shaped-human-history</link><description>&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/lewis-dartnell-on-origins-how-the-earth-shaped-human-history.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 14:50:42 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/lewis-dartnell-on-origins-how-the-earth-shaped-human-history</guid></item><item><title>图案板利用表面振动来移动和旋转物体，无需复杂的电子设备</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/patterned-plate-uses-surface-vibrations-to-move-and-spin-objects-without-complex-electronics</link><description>中国研究人员开发了一种利用特殊结构的振动来操纵固体表面上的物体的方法，允许粒子和其他小物体被限制、沿圆形路径移动或旋转，而无需通常需要产生这种运动的复杂电子控制系统。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/patterned-plate-uses-surface-vibrations-to-move-and-spin-objects-without-complex-electronics2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 14:35:42 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/patterned-plate-uses-surface-vibrations-to-move-and-spin-objects-without-complex-electronics</guid></item><item><title>当血涂片讲述故事时：诊断妊娠期致命的继发性噬血细胞性淋巴组织细胞增多症</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/when-a-blood-smear-tells-the-story-diagnosing-fatal-secondary-hemophagocytic-lymphohistiocytosis-in-pregnancy</link><description>埃塞俄比亚农村地区一名 20 岁的妇女在妊娠晚期出现发烧症状。她在几小时内就去世了。回头看看她的血涂片，答案一直就在那里。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/when-a-blood-smear-tells-the-story-diagnosing-fatal-secondary-hemophagocytic-lymphohistiocytosis-in-pregnancy.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 14:20:42 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/when-a-blood-smear-tells-the-story-diagnosing-fatal-secondary-hemophagocytic-lymphohistiocytosis-in-pregnancy</guid></item><item><title>P53 调节的非凋亡细胞死亡途径及其与癌症和其他疾病的相关性 评论 分子细胞生物学</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/p53-regulated-non-apoptotic-cell-death-pathways-and-their-relevance-in-cancer-and-other-diseases-reviews-molecular-cell-biology</link><description>肿瘤抑制因子 p53 控制非凋亡细胞死亡 (NACD) 途径，包括铁死亡、坏死性凋亡和细胞焦亡。本综述讨论了 NACD 受 p53 调节的作用、机制和生理环境，以及它们治疗人类疾病的潜在靶点。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/p53-regulated-non-apoptotic-cell-death-pathways-and-their-relevance-in-cancer-and-other-diseases-reviews-molecular-cell-biology.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 14:05:42 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/p53-regulated-non-apoptotic-cell-death-pathways-and-their-relevance-in-cancer-and-other-diseases-reviews-molecular-cell-biology</guid></item><item><title>肿瘤学中的心脏成像：心脏毒性的检测</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/cardiac-imaging-in-oncology-the-detection-of-cardiotoxicity</link><description>&lt;img src="https://politepaul.com/fd/dtDF30237DhP.xml" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 13:50:42 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/cardiac-imaging-in-oncology-the-detection-of-cardiotoxicity</guid></item><item><title>GLP-1 治疗时代的肥胖症多模式护理</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/multimodal-care-for-obesity-in-the-glp-1-therapy-era</link><description>这一观点敦促肥胖症的多模式管理，不仅限于药物治疗，还包括整个生命过程中的筛查、早期管理和强化行为治疗。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/multimodal-care-for-obesity-in-the-glp-1-therapy-era.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 13:35:42 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/multimodal-care-for-obesity-in-the-glp-1-therapy-era</guid></item><item><title>血管衰老是器官功能障碍和全身衰老的驱动因素</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/vascular-aging-as-a-driver-of-organ-dysfunction-and-systemic-aging</link><description>在这篇综述中，Dimmeler 和 Augustin 讨论了微血管衰老作为组织功能障碍和系统衰退的新兴关键驱动因素，强调单细胞和多组学方法如何揭示器官特异性血管脆弱性和信号机制，为血管年轻化和健康衰老开辟新的机会。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/vascular-aging-as-a-driver-of-organ-dysfunction-and-systemic-aging2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 13:20:42 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/vascular-aging-as-a-driver-of-organ-dysfunction-and-systemic-aging</guid></item><item><title>绘制了蓝斑去甲肾上腺素神经元！</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/locus-coeruleus-noradrenaline-neurons-mapped</link><description>背景：先兆子痫对胎儿脑血管生成产生不利影响，具有潜在的急性和长期后果。然而，这些脑血管改变的机制仍不清楚。我们研究了 TSP-1（凝血反应蛋白-1）（一种抗血管生成糖蛋白）是否介导先兆子痫中胎儿胎盘和胎儿脑内皮之间的通讯。方法：使用来自正常和先兆子痫妊娠的人脐静脉内皮细胞的条件培养基来处理人（人脑微血管内皮细胞系）和鼠脑内皮细胞。脐带血清的蛋白质组学分析鉴定出差异表达的蛋白质，并通过蛋白质印迹验证了 TSP-1。研究了脐带内皮细胞 (EA.&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/locus-coeruleus-noradrenaline-neurons-mapped2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 13:05:42 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/locus-coeruleus-noradrenaline-neurons-mapped</guid></item></channel></rss>